    "effectivePlan" : "Cross with C3 to CA and cash DQ, discarding a low spade. If diamonds divide 3-3, run D9 and D7, then return to South with a club to CK and cash HK for nine tricks. If DQ reveals a 4-2 break with DJ still outstanding, dummy's diamonds are not yet established and CA has already been spent. Lead D9 to force out DJ, retaining D7, and discard South's other low spade. The fallback then requires both an additional club trick and a club entry to dummy: regain control in South, cash CK with dummy following C4, and lead C7 toward CT, finessing against West's queen. If that succeeds, CT supplies the extra club trick and entry to D7; together with HK these provide nine tricks. A defensive club lead may resolve the finesse or establish CT earlier; adapt the order accordingly. This fallback is conditional on favorable club honors and the defenders not cashing five tricks first; there is no assured diamond entry after CA is spent. Preserve South's clubs and HK while testing diamonds.",
